Here’s the exact call you’d make to notify the routing‑nodes observer that the shard previously unassigned as **`shardA`** has moved into the initializing state **`shardB`**:

```java
// Notify the observer that an unassigned shard has become initializing
functions.RoutingNodesChangedObserver_shardInitialized(
    new java.util.HashMap<String, String>() {{
        put("unassignedShard", "shardA");
        put("initializedShard", "shardB");
    }}
);
```

**What this does**

- `unassignedShard` – the identifier of the shard that was previously unassigned (`shardA`).
- `initializedShard` – the identifier of the shard that is now in the initializing state (`shardB`).

When this method is invoked, the observer receives the update and can react accordingly (e.g., trigger allocation logic, update monitoring dashboards, etc.).
